{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287079-are-there-resources-for-help-in-designing-new-charms","id":1287079,"title":"Are there Resources for help in designing new charms?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-12T09:36:51-08:00","id":1287079,"title":"Are there Resources for help in designing new charms?","content":"Hi everyone, I really want to make my own homebrew charms for a variety of circumstances, particularly for Sidereal Martial Arts. However, unlike evocations and antagonists, I don't think I have much of a head for charm design and balance. Are there any resources for guidance in creating homebrew charms in terms of their power?<br /> <br /> As to the actual style I want to homebrew is the Kaleidoscopic Border of Logic Style, which was ... not great last edition. It either relied on overly costly and useless (beyond how royally it fucked with the victim) finishing blows and 'bad touches', or utterly broken scene long charms like its form and capstone. <br /> <br /> I want to turn into a style into something completely different. My version would ideally work by creating a Tulpa (thought-form) that is personalized through the style. The idea is highly inspired by stands from Jojo's Bizarre Adventure and will include a few shout-outs, as well as the Persona series. Where do you all think it should sit in terms of balance compared to Solar Charms? Should there be charms with essence beyond 5? I'm kind of worried about opening up exalted design space past 5. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","user":"Nabirius","date":".  more detail, and typos 02-12-2019, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T09:47:11-08:00","id":1287083,"title":"","content":"At the moment there aren\u2019t any official resources. However, the next hardcover after Lunars will be the Exigent Exalted book, which is slated to have a lot of useful charm design material in it.<br /> <br /> So far, in 3e, the plan is that Exalted charms only go up to essence 5, with some rare elders having the odd essence 6 trick. Sidereal Martial Arts are apparently going to abide by this rule as well, so it\u2019s hard to predict what they\u2019ll be like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 02-12-2019, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T09:50:45-08:00","id":1287089,"title":"","content":"There's no official resources for designing new charms, no. I do believe the Exigent book will have those, but that's still quite some time away.<br /> <br /> In any case, essence higher than 5 isn't really a thing anymore in this edition. So that's a &quot;no&quot; on charms requiring higher essence than that.<br /> <br /> IIRC, Vance mentioned most SMA will go from essence 3 to 5. Though that's early forecasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Let us take men and give them the favor of the gods and use them as our champions against the Primordials, that we might overthrow them and play for ourselves the Games of Divinity.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2272-senresk","name":"senresk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T10:18:11-08:00","id":1287094,"title":"","content":"I've got a very basic methodology to update mechanics to 3rd edition without a horrible fucking mess that I've been meaning to make into a flow diagram. Might try and get that done, it'll probably help some people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T10:32:48-08:00","id":1287097,"title":"","content":"Thanks! That's disappointing, so I may just make the style and then ask for feedback<br /> <br /> In terms of design, my initial idea was to start with the form charm that allowed the user to manifest the Tulpa, then have an interconnected tree of 20-25 charms, that the user could take 10-11 of, to build a personalized Tulpa. Then there was 1-3 essence 6 capstones that the user could choose one of. <br /> <br /> However, I'm not totally sold on this version. I could also consider a much more normal MA tree, again starting with the Form Charm which branches out into ways of using the Tulpa, with each charm giving a choice between 2-3 exclusive permanent effects to the tulpa's capabilities.<br /> <br /> The personalization of the form and function of the Tulpa, such that yours does not fight like anyone else's is a very important part of the design space to me. Are there other ways I could organize the tree?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T14:15:38-08:00","id":1287243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287079-are-there-resources-for-help-in-designing-new-charms?p=1287097#post1287097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! That's disappointing, so I may just make the style and then ask for feedback<br /> <br /> In terms of design, my initial idea was to start with the form charm that allowed the user to manifest the Tulpa, then have an interconnected tree of 20-25 charms, that the user could take 10-11 of, to build a personalized Tulpa. Then there was 1-3 essence 6 capstones that the user could choose one of.<br /> <br /> However, I'm not totally sold on this version. I could also consider a much more normal MA tree, again starting with the Form Charm which branches out into ways of using the Tulpa, with each charm giving a choice between 2-3 exclusive permanent effects to the tulpa's capabilities.<br /> <br /> The personalization of the form and function of the Tulpa, such that yours does not fight like anyone else's is a very important part of the design space to me. Are there other ways I could organize the tree?</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds less like a martial art to me and more like a type of Exalt or an Evocation tree. hmmm.....<br /> <br /> Maybe have a &quot;normal&quot; martial art, but it requires a secondary merit that covers the creation of the Tulpa and basically gives you an inbuilt artifact that can produce Evocations. So, the MA style forms the general effects, while the Evocations form the individualized Tulpa?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T17:25:41-08:00","id":1287349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287079-are-there-resources-for-help-in-designing-new-charms?p=1287243#post1287243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This sounds less like a martial art to me and more like a type of Exalt or an Evocation tree. hmmm.....<br /> <br /> Maybe have a &quot;normal&quot; martial art, but it requires a secondary merit that covers the creation of the Tulpa and basically gives you an inbuilt artifact that can produce Evocations. So, the MA style forms the general effects, while the Evocations form the individualized Tulpa?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really interesting idea, and it also covers the issue where I would want the Tulpa to be able to be manifested even when not in the Martial Arts Form in order to have more utility. One of the charms in the style has in my mind is 'Fate's Arrow' a decisive-only attack which either kills the target or grants them a Tulpa. It also might be good because then it can take on a larger variety of shapes and abilities. I'll play around with these ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T10:13:59-08:00","id":1288318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>senresk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287079-are-there-resources-for-help-in-designing-new-charms?p=1287089#post1287089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, essence higher than 5 isn't really a thing anymore in this edition. So that's a &amp;quot;no&amp;quot; on charms requiring higher essence than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That can be possibly misleading for new players. In the core book, there are Essence 6 Solar charm upgrades and other charms go up to Essence 7, so although Essence was dialed back, there is some uncharted space higher up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T12:10:08-08:00","id":1288352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287079-are-there-resources-for-help-in-designing-new-charms?p=1288318#post1288318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That can be possibly misleading for new players. In the core book, there are Essence 6 Solar charm upgrades and other charms go up to Essence 7, so although Essence was dialed back, there is some uncharted space higher up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait, I missed this, what were the essence 6 charms in core, and where were the essence 7 charms period? Ahlat is Essence 7 but I don't know that his charms have minimums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T16:01:03-08:00","id":1288769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287079-are-there-resources-for-help-in-designing-new-charms?p=1288352#post1288352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wait, I missed this, what were the essence 6 charms in core, and where were the essence 7 charms period? Ahlat is Essence 7 but I don't know that his charms have minimums.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are Essence 6 repurchases for Searing Sunfire Interdiction (p 259) and Essence 6 bonus effects for Shadow-Crossing Leap Technique (p 408). I don't know about any Essence 7 effects, though. I was working on the assumption that those effects are basically only available to Archery/Stealth supernal characters. Only, I just remembered that it doesn't disregard the essence prerequisite, it just treats your essence as 5 for that ability's charms. Sooooo... I guess it does imply that Essence 6 will be permissible in a future supplement or something.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}